# Phase 900: Throwaway Codex Dogfood Target - Pattern Map

**Mapped:** 2026-08-27
**Files analyzed:** 2 (1 new, 1 one-line edit)
**Analogs found:** 2 / 2

## File Classification

| New/Modified File | Role | Data Flow | Closest Analog | Match Quality |
|-------------------|------|-----------|----------------|---------------|
| `crates/devflow-core/src/dogfood_scratch.rs` (NEW) | utility (leaf module) | transform (pure fn) | `crates/devflow-core/src/stage.rs` (module shape + inline tests) + `crates/devflow-core/src/phase_id.rs` (pure free fn + `#[must_use]`) | role-match (composite) |
| `crates/devflow-core/src/lib.rs` (MODIFY, 1 line) | config (module list) | — | its own existing `pub mod` list, lines 54-86 | exact |

## Pattern Assignments

### `crates/devflow-core/src/dogfood_scratch.rs` (utility, pure transform)

**Analog A — module doc + inline test module:** `crates/devflow-core/src/stage.rs`
**Analog B — pure free function with `#[must_use]` + `///` docs:** `crates/devflow-core/src/phase_id.rs`

**Module doc-comment style** (`stage.rs:1-8`) — `//!` block, one-line summary then a blank `//!` line then prose:
```rust
//! DevFlow stage machine.
//!
//! The workflow is a single linear chain of five stages:
//! Define → Plan → Code → Validate → Ship.
```

**Pure free function with `#[must_use]` + `///` doc** (`phase_id.rs:145-154`) — `///` doc describes the return and the reject/guard case; attribute directly above `fn`; single guarded expression as the body, no `Result`:
```rust
/// Parses one dot-separated component.
///
/// Rejects anything `u32::from_str` would accept but a path or branch name
/// should not — notably a leading `+`, which `"+5".parse::<u32>()` accepts.
fn component(part: &str) -> Option<u32> {
    if part.is_empty() || !part.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_digit()) {
        return None;
    }
    part.parse::<u32>().ok()
}
```
`#[must_use]` placement on a small pure fn (`phase_id.rs:38-42`):
```rust
    /// An integer-numbered phase, e.g. `35`.
    #[must_use]
    pub const fn new(major: u32) -> Self {
        Self { major, minor: None }
    }
```
Guard-then-single-stdlib-call is exactly the body shape RESEARCH.md prescribes (`if bucket_size == 0 { return 0; }` then `item_count.div_ceil(bucket_size)`), and it matches `component`'s early-return-then-one-expression form.

**Inline `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` pattern** (`stage.rs:104-115`, identical in `phase_id.rs:231-238`) — `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { use super::*; ... }`, one `#[test]` fn with a descriptive snake_case name, body is a run of plain `assert_eq!` calls on fixed inputs (include the zero-guard case as its own assertion):
```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn next_walks_linear_chain_then_terminates() {
        assert_eq!(Stage::Define.next(), Some(Stage::Plan));
        assert_eq!(Stage::Plan.next(), Some(Stage::Code));
        assert_eq!(Stage::Ship.next(), None);
    }
}
```

**Do NOT copy from these analogs:** `serde` derives, `thiserror` error structs, `impl Display`/`FromStr`, enums — `stage.rs` and `phase_id.rs` have all of these and none belong in this module (RESEARCH.md anti-patterns: no enum, no `Result`, no error plumbing, no new `use`).

---

### `crates/devflow-core/src/lib.rs` (config, module list)

**Analog:** the file's own `pub mod` list (`lib.rs:54-86`), which is strictly alphabetical by module name.

**Current state** (`lib.rs:59-61`):
```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod doc_check;
pub mod events;
```

**Edit — insert one line** (`doc` < `dog` < `eve`, so it sorts between `doc_check` and `events`):
```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod doc_check;
pub mod dogfood_scratch;
pub mod events;
```
`pub mod` (not `mod`) — matches every non-test sibling in the list. Do NOT add a re-export in the `// Re-exports for convenience.` block (`lib.rs:88-91`).

## Shared Patterns

### Rust module conventions (whole crate)
**Source:** `crates/devflow-core/src/stage.rs`, `crates/devflow-core/src/phase_id.rs`
**Apply to:** the new module
- `//!` module doc: one-line summary, blank `//!`, then prose.
- `///` doc on every `pub` item.
- `#[must_use]` immediately above `pub fn` when the fn exists for its return value.
- Tests live inline in the same file: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { use super::*; ... }` with `#[test]` fns using plain `assert_eq!`.
- No `TODO` comments; run `cargo fmt` before commit; body must already be the form clippy wants (single guarded stdlib call — see RESEARCH.md "Don't Hand-Roll": use `u64::div_ceil`, never `(a + b - 1) / b`).

## No Analog Found

None. Both files have strong in-crate analogs.

